1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,250
Narrator：Listen to a podcast on health.

2
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:03,588
Do you have trouble sleeping at night?

3
00:00:03,588 --> 00:00:05,180
Then maybe this is for you.

4
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:10,182
When you worry about needing sleep and toss and turn trying to find a

5
00:00:10,182 --> 00:00:13,040
comfortable position, you're probably only making matters worse.

6
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:17,579
What happens when you do that, is that your heart rate actually increases, making

7
00:00:17,579 --> 00:00:19,200
it more difficult to relax.

8
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,869
You may also have some bad habits that contribute to the problem.

9
00:00:22,869 --> 00:00:25,010
Do you rest frequently during the day?

10
00:00:25,010 --> 00:00:27,030
Do you get virtually no exercise,

11
00:00:27,030 --> 00:00:30,060
or do you exercise strenuously late in the day?

12
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:31,743
Are you preoccupied with sleep,

13
00:00:31,743 --> 00:00:34,100
or do you sleep late on weekends?

14
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:38,264
Any or all of these factors might be leading to your insomnia by disrupting

15
00:00:38,264 --> 00:00:39,453
your body's natural rhythm.

16
00:00:39,453 --> 00:00:42,130
What should you do, then, on those sleepless nights?

17
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:44,201
Don't bother with sleeping pills.

18
00:00:44,201 --> 00:00:47,100
They can actually cause worse insomnia later.

19
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:51,519
The best thing to do is drink milk or eat cheese or tuna fish.

20
00:00:51,519 --> 00:00:55,938
These are all rich in amino acids and help produce a neurotransmitter in the

21
00:00:55,938 --> 00:00:57,200
brain that induces sleep.

22
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,150
This neurotransmitter will help you relax,

23
00:00:59,150 --> 00:01:03,050
and you'll be on your way to getting a good night's sleep.

24
00:01:03,050 --> 00:01:08,070
Until tomorrow's broadcast, this has been another in the series "Hints for Good Health."
